IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-54. NOUNS of a cross-reference. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Consumer Protection Law, 5741-1981. It records citations: for each, what the citing words are about,
-- what the words they use find at the other end, and where each reading comes from. A citation whose two descriptions differ is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from the citing words and from the text at the other end,
-- so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind. The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module
-- (`src:N` lines are line N of the deposited consolidation excerpt; `ext:[SH ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `the paragraph on warranty certificates, paragraph (5) of subsection (א) of section 18א`
    `paragraph (5) of section 18א as a bare address: two paragraphs carry that number, one in subsection (א) and one in subsection (א1), and the section has no paragraph (5) at its top level`
    `the paragraph on repair and replacement of goods, paragraph (1) of subsection (א) of section 18א`
    `paragraph (1) of section 18א as a bare address: at least three paragraphs carry that number, in subsections (א), (א1) and (ג), and the section has no paragraph (1) at its top level`
    `subsection (א1) of section 18א, the warranty sticker`
    `subsection (ד) of section 17ב, the binding price of goods`
    `the short name that item 1 of the Second Schedule defines for the Communications Law (Bezeq and Broadcasts), 5742-1982`
    `item 1 of the Second Schedule as section 105 of the Communications (Broadcasts) Law, 5786-2026, rewrites it: it defines a short name for the Bezeq Law and defines no short name for the Communications Law`
    `the short name of the Bezeq Law as item 1 of the Second Schedule defines it once section 105 of the Communications (Broadcasts) Law, 5786-2026, has taken effect`

-- Three kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest.
-- The second kind is the honest name for most limbs here: the official page was read, but that no LATER instrument touched the words rests on the consolidation.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the citing words take effect on before any postponement` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the citing words take effect no later than if every postponement is used` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the words stop reaching their text on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `read in context the citing words reach` IS A MAYBE `What a provision is about`
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
